ntum symmetry of graph $C^{*}$-algebras has been explored by several mathematicians within different categories in the past few years. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBiologically Inspired Self-Organizing Computational Model to Mimic Infant Learning (https://doi.org/10.3390/make5020030)\nciteturn13search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3.5 years ago; Crawled: 3 months ago; Centre for Automation and Robotics, Hindustan Institute of Technology and Science, Chennai 603103, India\n\nImageKuppan Chetty Ramanathan\n\nSciProfiles Scilit Preprints.org Google Scholar\n\n^{ 1}\n\n^{1}\n\nCentre for Automation and Robotics, Hindustan Institute of Technology and Science, Chennai 603103, India\n\n^{2}\n\nSchool of Computing Sciences, Agurchand Manmull Jain College, Chennai 600114, India\n\n^{*}\n\nAuthor to whom correspondence should be addressed.\n\nMach. Learn. Knowl. Extr. 2023, 5(2), 491-511; https://doi.org/10.3390/make5020030\n\nSubmission received: 10 April 2023 / Revised: 27 April 2023 / Accepted: 6 May 2023 / Published: 15 May 2023\n\n(This article belongs to the Section Learning)\n\nDownload keyboard_arrow_down\n\nDownload PDF\nDownload PDF with Cover\nDownload XML\nDownload Epub\n\nBrowse Figures\n\nVersions Notes\n\n## Abstract\n\nRecent technological advancements have fostered human–robot coexistence in work and residential environments. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n(PDF) A new matrix representation of the Maxwell equations based on the Riemann-Silberstein-Weber vector for a linear inhomogeneous medium (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/360782190_A_new_matrix_representation_of_the_Maxwell_equations_based_on_the_Riemann-Silberstein-Weber_vector_for_a_linear_inhomogeneous_medium)\nciteturn13search6 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4.4 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; # A new matrix representation of the Maxwell equations based on the Riemann-Silberstein-Weber vector for a linear inhomogeneous medium ... DOI:10.48550/arXiv.2205.09907 ... Tharamani, Chennai 600113, India\nPreprint PDF Available\n\n# A new matrix representation of the Maxwell equations based on the Riemann-Silberstein-Weber vector for a linear inhomogeneous medium\n\n  * May 2022\n\nDOI:10.48550/arXiv.2205.09907\n\n  * License\n  * CC BY 4.0\n\nAuthors:\n\nSameen Ahmed Khan\n\n  * Dhofar University\n\nRamaswamy Jagannathan\n\n  * Institute of Mathematical Sciences\n\nImage\n\nDownload file PDFRead file\n\n\n## Abstract\n\nAn eight-dimensional matrix representation of the Maxwell equations for a linear inhomogeneous medium has been obtained earlier based on the Riemann-Silberstein-Weber vector starting from the equations satisfied by it. A new eight-dimensional matrix representation, related to the earlier one by a similarity transformation, is derived starting ab initio from the Maxwell equations. The new representation has a more advantageous structure compared to the earlier one from the point of view of applications. In the case of a homogeneous medium the new matrix representation reduces to a block diagonal form with four two-dimensional Pauli matrix blocks along the diagonal. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nANNUAL REPORT 2024-25 (https://www.iitm.ac.in/sites/default/files/Others/Annual%20Report%202024-25%20final%20upload.pdf)\nciteturn13search14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 10 months ago; Bent Weber, School of Physical and Mathematical Sciences, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore</td> ... <td>Chennai Soft Matter Day</td> ... <td>Eccentricity Workshop - Challenges in Unravelling Astrophysical Eccentric Compact Binaries</td>\nANNUAL REPORT 2024-25  \n4.18. DEPARTMENT OF PHYSICS\n\n<table id=\"e1\">\n<tr>\n<th>Name and Qualifications</th>\n<th>Major Areas of Specialisation</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Prof. Bent Weber, School of Physical and Mathematical Sciences, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore